: How do I convert a good altar to Crom?

Pardon if modus orperandi says that answers are emailed rather than
posted, but in case this is not the fact I will answer.

I have been able to convert a non aligned altar (ie, an altar belonging
to another god) into an aligned altar by sacrificing a non nuetral
creature on the altar in question.   I've seen one of two results
immediately after the sacrifice.  First it says something to the effect
of "your god struggles with the other god".  Then either your god wins or 
the other god wins.  If your god wins I suppose you get brownie points and
the other god sends a creature to attack you.   After this there is no
more retribution.  If your god loses then.... well, that's not good.

I think I remember that by sacrificing a co aligned unicorn on a non
co aligned altar you are attempting an alignment change. 
 
I believe that the gnarlier the creature the better chance your god has
to win the struggle, so try sacrificing something totally heinous.

